README-NEWS -- three news systems, and which one to takeIf you are setting up Usenet news on your own OS-9 system you want ONE newssystem.  This file is here so you do not have to install all three to findout how they differ.Short answer: take MNews with nn if you want to read news in comfort.  nnhas threads, kill files and online help, MNews needs no Microware module,and all of it is built from the source on this disk.  Take C News with rnif you want the Unix pair -- C News's relay and Larry Wall's reader.  Take UUCPbb's news if you alreadyrun UUCPbb for mail and want the small set that lives beside it.THE THREE---------                   UUCPbb 2.1 news     C News + rn         MNews + nn  ------------------------------------------------------------------------  directory        CMDS/UUCP           CMDS/NEWS           CMDS/MNEWS  programs         6                   12                  11, and `setup'  bytes            116146              342080              410646  needs cio        yes, all six        the six tools only  no  files articles   rnews               relaynews           inews (rnews                                                           hands on to it)  reader           readnews: prompts   rn: full screen     nn: full screen  posts            postnews            Pnews               inews, nnaux  spool            SPOOL/news          SPOOL/CNEWS         SPOOL/MNEWS  article names    COMP/OS/OS9/a1      junk/1              comp/os/os9/1  active file in   SYS/UUCP            USR/LIB/CNEWS       USR/LIB/NEWS  your place       .newsrc             .newsrc             .nn/rc  source           SRC/uucpbb          SRC/cnews, SRC/rn43 SRC/mnews  docs             DOC/uucpbb          DOC/cnews, DOC/rn   DOC/mnews, DOC/nn  UUCPbb   rnews 22348, readnews 33162, postnews 26526, expire 15472,           subscribe 9308, unsubscribe 9330.  Bob Billson's, GPL v2.  C News   relaynews 66142; bdecode 8818, byteflip 1882, c7decode 2304,   